an="1">1.27 (0.38&#x02013;4.27)</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>p-value trend</italic><xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="nt116">*</xref></td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>0.107</italic></td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>0.310</italic></td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>0.417</italic></td></tr></tbody></table></alternatives><table-wrap-foot><fn id="nt112"><label>&#x02020;</label><p>&#x02013; Age as a continuous variable,</p></fn><fn id="nt113"><label>&#x02021;</label><p>&#x02013;WHR as a continuous variable,</p></fn><fn id="nt114"><label>&#x000b6;</label><p>&#x02013; NSAID use as a categorical variable (Current, Former, never),</p></fn><fn id="nt115"><label>&#x020ac;</label><p>&#x02013; Smoking as a categorical variable (Ever, never).</p></fn><fn id="nt116"><label>*</label><p>Test for trend was based on the likelihood-ratio test associated with addition of the variable under consideration in its continuous form.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="pone-0052192-t005" orientation="portrait" position="float"><object-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1371/journal.pone.0052192.t005</object-id><label>Table 5</label><caption><title>Adjusted hazard ratios (HRs) and 95% confidence intervals (CIs) of esophageal adenocarcinoma (EA) for BMI and waist-hip ratio (WHR) in the SBES cohort.</title></caption><alternatives><graphic id="pone-0052192-t005-5" xlink:href="pone.0052192.t005"/><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><colgroup span="1"><col align="left" span="1"/><col align="center" span="1"/><col align="center" span="1"/><col align="center" span="1"/><col align="center" span="1"/></colgroup><thead><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">EA/total</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Unadjusted HR(95% CI)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Adjusted for age<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="nt117">&#x02020;</xref> and gender HR(95% CI)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Adjusted for age<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="nt117">&#x02020;</xref>, gender, cigarette smoking<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="nt118">&#x02021;</xref> and NSAID<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="nt119">&#x000b6;</xref> use HR(95% CI)</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>BMI</bold></td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">BMI continuous</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">45/397</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.99 (0.93&#x02013;1.07)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.02 (0.95&#x02013;1.10)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.01 (0.94&#x02013;1.10)</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">BMI categories</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02264;25</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">6/54</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">REF</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">REF</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">REF</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003e;25-&#x02264;30</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">22/188</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.91 (0.37&#x02013;2.24)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.00 (0.40&#x02013;2.49)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.88 (0.35&#x02013;2.19)</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003e;30-&#x02264;35</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">13/120</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.84 (0.32&#x02013;2.22)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.99 (0